            {
                "entry_id": "f57758bb-91ff-3e04-8ef2-241c4097f748",
                "word": "élagable",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e4f08b2a-5f2c-4c08-83b1-140a89d75851",
                        "entry_id": "f57758bb-91ff-3e04-8ef2-241c4097f748",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "élagables"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f872d050-b5a7-3cf5-9944-20f7890096de",
                        "entry_id": "f57758bb-91ff-3e04-8ef2-241c4097f748",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Que l’on peut élaguer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "314fad0c-3aae-43dd-bfc3-21b4ba9308ef",
                                "sense_id": "f872d050-b5a7-3cf5-9944-20f7890096de",
                                "text": "Le baliveau est un arbre d’avenir, choisi parmi les essences capables de produire du bois d’œuvre de qualité. Il se caractérise par un tronc droit, à section circulaire, élagué ou élagable sur 6 à 8 mètres, sans défauts apparents, et un houppier bien équilibré."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "98548914-1166-36c9-a9c1-4c0553ae4741",
                        "entry_id": "f57758bb-91ff-3e04-8ef2-241c4097f748",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui peut être coupé, retranché."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1cc25601-5270-469a-b185-dc8ca5a23e94",
                                "sense_id": "98548914-1166-36c9-a9c1-4c0553ae4741",
                                "text": "D’ailleurs il était pauvre et, par conséquent, élagable..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1e8281a-fea7-49c3-802f-7b5683201d80",
                                "sense_id": "98548914-1166-36c9-a9c1-4c0553ae4741",
                                "text": "On a généralement moins abordé la critique d’un aspect plus profond, moins facilement élagable de l’œuvre proprement scientifique : le fait de considérer les tendances découvertes dans l’exploration des faits comme principe, primum movens, de la vie mentale de l’individu ou de la vie sociale."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "6bfcdc98-aca0-3f91-8118-5108d8dd5688",
                "word": "Élagable",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4d507898-1a7e-4add-8f3b-35913a32a6f2",
                        "entry_id": "6bfcdc98-aca0-3f91-8118-5108d8dd5688",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "Élagabal"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "fbbe368b-5e02-479e-9cd4-3db9abfc75f5",
                        "entry_id": "6bfcdc98-aca0-3f91-8118-5108d8dd5688",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "Héliogabale"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fce3cc9e-6832-3c9c-8a7b-d85eba8e3ea1",
                        "entry_id": "6bfcdc98-aca0-3f91-8118-5108d8dd5688",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nom désignant l’empereur romain né Varius Avitus Bassianus."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bbd40476-6bc5-452d-bb39-c7a5ad0a93c0",
                                "sense_id": "fce3cc9e-6832-3c9c-8a7b-d85eba8e3ea1",
                                "text": "Elle reçut apparemment de nouvelles graces de Caracalla, puisqu’elle prit en son honneur le titre d’Antonianum, qu’on lit sur les médailles de Cæla, frappées sous le regne de ce Prince, & sous ceux d’Élagable, de Sévere Alexandre & de Maximin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af38165b-9b5a-4efb-b0e7-56eed889224d",
                                "sense_id": "fce3cc9e-6832-3c9c-8a7b-d85eba8e3ea1",
                                "text": "Mais on peut observer que la plupart des successeurs d’Élagable renoncèrent à ce luxe asiatique."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8fd112b2-6d17-41d7-b88a-72b9bfc5b868",
                                "sense_id": "fce3cc9e-6832-3c9c-8a7b-d85eba8e3ea1",
                                "text": "Doit-on pour autant oublier que l’acclimatation du culte du Soleil sous des formes non mithriaques a été tentée par plusieurs empereurs, Aurélien et Élagable en particulier ?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "01258051-927a-4cd7-8933-a9a04cbd697d",
                        "source_entry_id": "6bfcdc98-aca0-3f91-8118-5108d8dd5688",
                        "source_sense_id": "fce3cc9e-6832-3c9c-8a7b-d85eba8e3ea1",
                        "target_lang_word": "Elagabal",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Elagabal",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0dfa71d6-0de5-3a9a-bf75-b0601846d267",
                                        "entry_id": "6d18b219-bc83-3984-9140-b9de32e442e9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "antiker semitischer Sonnengott"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6aaea9af-af51-445f-b082-e23adb72584f",
                                                "sense_id": "0dfa71d6-0de5-3a9a-bf75-b0601846d267",
                                                "text": "„Im Zentrum erhob sich ein mit Juwelen besetzter Prachttempel, der dem semitischen Sonnengott Elagabal gewidmet war.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c19fd463-f645-398e-aa75-f69a73b38c2b",
                                        "entry_id": "6d18b219-bc83-3984-9140-b9de32e442e9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "römischer Kaiser im 3. Jahrhundert nach Christus, der in der Neuzeit als Sinnbild für die Lasterhaftigkeit der römischen Kaiserzeit gilt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2d2236d-ea0c-4373-a711-d9456ffb0b20",
                                                "sense_id": "c19fd463-f645-398e-aa75-f69a73b38c2b",
                                                "text": "„Nero war mit 17, Commodus mit 16 und Elagabal mit 14 Jahren Kaiser geworden.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "980416b6-dcc8-4aa4-868e-2e49e3e6f01f",
                        "source_entry_id": "6bfcdc98-aca0-3f91-8118-5108d8dd5688",
                        "source_sense_id": "fce3cc9e-6832-3c9c-8a7b-d85eba8e3ea1",
                        "target_lang_word": "Elagabalus",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Elagabalus",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "54c67ede-eada-3f96-b6da-e9d5dad52ab5",
                                        "entry_id": "b2781e4d-efac-3b83-bc2a-28ab0f34932a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The deity Elagabal, venerated in ancient times at Emesa in Syria (and later elsewhere in the Roman Empire), identified with a large black stone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7b14bfb-944a-42c9-80f7-405292f03231",
                                                "sense_id": "54c67ede-eada-3f96-b6da-e9d5dad52ab5",
                                                "text": "Elagabalus, who was a Sun-god and the patron deity of Emesa, was worshipped […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3481e1e-1208-4d83-a08e-66e81f3203f3",
                                                "sense_id": "54c67ede-eada-3f96-b6da-e9d5dad52ab5",
                                                "text": "Obviously, they hoped to conceal the failure of their unhappy experiment in emperorship before, when they stressed the priesthood of Syrian Emesa's main deity Elagabalus as the key factor […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0f4a607-afd4-3d5c-884c-d84edd41282e",
                                        "entry_id": "b2781e4d-efac-3b83-bc2a-28ab0f34932a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The Roman emperor Marcus Aurelius Antoninus Augustus (reigned 218–222), noted for eccentricity, femininity, decadence, and disregard for Roman religious traditions and sexual taboos."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ancient-Rome"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13a5d75f-bf0e-4f97-be39-e85229e9c013",
                                                "sense_id": "d0f4a607-afd4-3d5c-884c-d84edd41282e",
                                                "text": "Racial prejudice also played a part, says Icks: before coming to Rome to rule it, Elagabalus was a priest in an obscure cult in Syria that venerated a black stone meteorite – a culture that would have been deeply strange to the Romans."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
